title Caravan reclaim -- a conferral leaves with the dependent it was made to
prompt Kyri first, then REMEMBER and the road-ahead itineraries; Standfast on reds, then the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; council rota one doc; condense REMEMBER when a set closes; send each finished increment
think Standfast first. The living REDS rows read whole: %90 closed by the host rebuild last lap, %91 superseded by %93 and %94 and released with the 514-page room sweep, %88 %89 %92 all closed on metal. No agent-closable red stands open, so the corrective queue is empty and the constructive one may open.
think The road ahead names the Lindy-priority Microkernel Target double-seat ahead of Seasons A-H, and its Equinox 1 is Caravan on the microkernel. Forty-five green rings stood. The newest rung, revoke.rye, closed the back half of a standing dependent's life and named no successor question, so the crux had to be found rather than read off a list.
think Reading confer and revoke together, the hole is plain and it is structural rather than stylistic. A conferral is published per domain -- words, count, and answers -- and a domain outlives every dependent that ever stands in it. Revocation prunes the holder's hands; the word on the wire is untouched. So the next dependent of that domain grafts a live capability no door ever weighed for it.
think That is the third member of a family the arc already half-named: dark reach before the door weighed it, stale reach after the work came home, inherited reach at a first breath. Naming it that way made the whole rung fall out -- the measurement, the refusals, and the control run that shows the hazard rather than asserting it.
think The plan is four phases and the successor is the whole of it. client_a stands with a reserve, a peek phase confers menu to it and the run revokes it again, then a second client_a stands with a reserve of its own and no phase confers anything to it. Under the leaving take it comes home having grafted one word anyway.
think The first cut of the measurement was wrong, and measuring is what said so. The elder reported its own conferral as inherited, because a supervisor may write for a dependent between the spawn and its first breath, so something standing on the wire is no evidence at all. The fix is that a conferral names the generation it was made to, and only a word addressed to an earlier generation counts.
think The generation is a measurement, never a guard, and saying so plainly is the honest part. A careless successor grafts a foreign word whether or not it is labelled, so the reclamation is what makes the hazard impossible; the label only makes it visible. A rung that confused the two would be claiming an isolation it does not have.
think A reclamation takes the conferral whole -- words, count, address, and every answer about it. Clearing the count alone would be enough for reach, yet a stale answer of held would let a supervisor believe a successor grafted a word it never saw, so defense in depth is cheap here and named rather than assumed.
think Five RED paths proven on metal before any GREEN. Two of them needed care: dropping a refusal outright made the parameter unused and the build refused, which is not a proof of anything, so the condition was falsified in place instead and the fold went RED for the right reason.
think REDS %81's lesson applied without being asked -- the rung is registered in caravan_suite_witness, so the choir's bijection stays whole at 53 and a rung that proves itself is never invisible to the one check built to see it.
think TAME's ratchet printed run_in_take at 71 lines, one past the bound, so it split at its natural seam -- seat_the_ground now provisions the regions, bells, notes, and capability table before any dependent is spawned, and the supervisor reads shorter for it.
obs The rung buys no speed and no room, exactly as revoke and confer did not. It buys the third quarter of the isolation claim, and the arc now answers what a dependent may touch before the door weighs it, while it stands, after its work comes home, and after it is gone.
obs What made this crux findable was reading the two rungs below as a pair rather than as a list. Neither is wrong; together they describe a dependent's whole life except its aftermath, and the aftermath is where a capability system usually leaks.
obs The council rota read this lap was item 8, the Singularity foundation. Its line about the mirror misaligned -- that a tool which builds itself is trustworthy only because it can also catch itself -- is what this round did in miniature when the elder's inherited count disagreed with the design and the design lost.
obs The REMEMBER condense was due rather than optional. Eight prior-live-edge bullets stood inline while every one of them lives in a dated log, in caravan/README.md, or in the REDS ledger, so the card had become a second copy of the record. Cairn 684f5ade97 first, then the fold.
loom witness=caravan_reclaim_witness rungs=53 phases=4 dependents=3 conferred=1 revoked=1 inherited_left_behind=1 inherited_reclaimed=0 red_paths_proven=5
file caravan/reclaim.rye the rung -- inherited reach, the generation a conferral is addressed to, four refusals, and the reclamation that takes a conferral whole
file tools/caravan_reclaim_witness.rish the witness on metal, reading the selftest natively and naming all five proven RED paths
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish the choir registration, so the bijection stands at 53 and no rung sings unheard
file caravan/README.md the durable record of the rung, beside confer and revoke, in the same commit as the code it describes
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge seated and eight prior edges folded to one pointer, so the card stays single-stranded
file crux/CAIRNS.md the walk-back nib recorded before the fold swept the card
recommend keep-going the arc's next question is already visible from this rung -- a dependent that falls holding conferred reach can answer for nothing, so reclamation on a decline is the mirror of this rung the way this rung is the mirror of revoke.
